        "citation": "DGS 008038536, item 4, local image 105 of 123. Máximo Basquez and Josefa Ribera married in Humacao on 31 December 1805. Máximo was the legitimate son of Francisco and María Cortez; Josefa was the legitimate daughter of Luís and Isidora Rodríguez. The record does not state surnames for Francisco or Luís. The three banns disclosed no impediment; the couple received Penitence and Eucharist, while nuptial blessings were deferred because the marriage occurred during a prohibited time. Witnesses were Don Máximo López and Don Manuel Eliza.",
